---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/asbj41.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Consolidating Previously Scattered Guidance" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Adjusting vs Non-Adjusting Events" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Approval Date — the Key Reference Point" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Going Concern Reassessment" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Why This Standard Was Needed — Systematising Previously Dispersed Rules" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — an Adjusting Event" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — a Non-Adjusting Event" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <LifecycleNotice
    type="effective-soon"
    title="Exposure Draft (January 2026)"
    explanation="STATUS NOTE: This Statement was released as an EXPOSURE DRAFT on January 9, 2026, with a proposed effective date for fiscal years beginning on or after April 1, 2027. Confirmation against ASBJ's final published standard is recommended upon formal adoption."
    link=""
    linkText=""
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A single, dedicated standard replacing scattered auditing-committee-report guidance</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 41 addresses events OCCURRING AFTER the balance sheet date but BEFORE the financial statements are APPROVED for issue — determining WHETHER such events should trigger an ADJUSTMENT to the financial statements THEMSELVES, or merely a DISCLOSURE. Previously, Japan's subsequent events guidance was SCATTERED across Auditing Standards Committee Reports and general accounting principles, WITHOUT a single, dedicated ACCOUNTING standard — this Statement CONSOLIDATES and SYSTEMATISES that guidance while ALIGNING it with IAS 10 internationally.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope — Consolidating Previously Scattered Guidance</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">All companies preparing financial statements under J-GAAP</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies preparing financial statements, addressing events between the BALANCE SHEET date and the date financial statements are APPROVED for issue.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Adjusting vs Non-Adjusting Events</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Evidence of conditions at the balance sheet date, versus new conditions arising after</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-1-2">
            <span>Event type</span>
            <span>Treatment</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-2">
            <span>Adjusting event</span>
            <span>Provides EVIDENCE of conditions that EXISTED at the balance sheet date — the financial statements are ADJUSTED to reflect this evidence</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-1-2">
            <span>Non-adjusting event</span>
            <span>Indicative of conditions that AROSE AFTER the balance sheet date — DISCLOSED only, with NO adjustment to recognised amounts</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This TWO-CATEGORY framework directly MIRRORS IAS 10's own adjusting/non-adjusting event distinction internationally.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>The Approval Date — the Key Reference Point</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Defining precisely when the subsequent events window closes</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The subsequent events REVIEW period runs from the balance sheet date UNTIL the date the financial statements are APPROVED for issue (typically board approval, 承認日) — a PRECISE reference point this Statement seeks to CLARIFY and make CONSISTENT across preparers, addressing PRACTICAL questions such as HOW to treat information arriving from SUBSIDIARIES close to the parent's OWN approval deadline.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>Going Concern Reassessment</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A subsequent event can fundamentally change the basis of preparation</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Where a subsequent event INDICATES that the GOING CONCERN basis of preparation is NO LONGER appropriate (e.g. a decision to LIQUIDATE, or cease TRADING, arising AFTER the balance sheet date), this represents the MOST SIGNIFICANT possible category of adjusting-type consequence — REQUIRING a FUNDAMENTAL change to the basis on which the ENTIRE financial statements are prepared, RATHER than a narrow, isolated adjustment.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Why This Standard Was Needed — Systematising Previously Dispersed Rules</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Clarifying the basis for existing practice, not overhauling it</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Commentary on this exposure draft has NOTED that the NEW standard is NOT expected to SUBSTANTIALLY change existing PRACTICE — Japanese companies have ALREADY been applying broadly SIMILAR principles through auditing-standards-committee guidance and general accounting PRINCIPLES. Rather, this Statement's PRIMARY value lies in providing a CLEAR, SYSTEMATIC, dedicated ACCOUNTING basis for treatment that was PREVIOUSLY scattered and less FORMALLY codified — REDUCING the risk of INCONSISTENT judgement across preparers.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — an Adjusting Event</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Reflecting evidence of a condition that already existed</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A major customer's bankruptcy confirming an existing receivable's impairment</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company's fiscal year ends March 31. On April 20 (before board approval), a major customer with an outstanding receivable at March 31 files for bankruptcy, confirming the customer had already been in serious financial distress AT the balance sheet date.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">This is an ADJUSTING EVENT — the bankruptcy filing PROVIDES EVIDENCE of a condition (the customer's financial distress) that ALREADY EXISTED at March 31. The company ADJUSTS its financial statements, recognising an IMPAIRMENT of the receivable AS AT the balance sheet date.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — a Non-Adjusting Event</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Disclosure only, no adjustment to recognised amounts</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A fire destroying a warehouse after year end</div>
          <div class="wk-body">The SAME company's warehouse is destroyed by a fire on April 25 — an event with NO connection to conditions existing at the March 31 balance sheet date.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">This is a NON-ADJUSTING EVENT — the fire is INDICATIVE of a condition ARISING AFTER the balance sheet date. The company DISCLOSES the nature of the event and, WHERE practicable, an estimate of its FINANCIAL effect, WITHOUT adjusting the RECOGNISED amounts in the March 31 financial statements themselves.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 41 (as proposed) requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>The date financial statements were approved for issue</span>
          <span>Nature of material non-adjusting events, and an estimate of their financial effect (or a statement that such an estimate cannot be made)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Distinguishing adjusting from non-adjusting events</span>
              <span>Whether a subsequent event undermines the going concern basis of preparation</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Estimated financial effect of a material non-adjusting event, where practicable to determine</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP (as proposed) vs IAS 10</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Feature</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 41, proposed)</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IAS 10)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Adjusting/non-adjusting distinction</span>
            <span>YES</span>
            <span>YES — converged</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Going concern reassessment</span>
            <span>YES</span>
            <span>YES — converged</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This Statement is a DELIBERATE, EXPLICIT convergence project — ASBJ's OWN commentary on the exposure draft specifically CITES alignment with IAS 10 as a core OBJECTIVE, alongside the domestic goal of CONSOLIDATING previously scattered rules.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every subsequent event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Adjusting event</span>
            <span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span>
            <span>Recognised amounts adjusted</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Non-adjusting event</span>
            <span>Notes only</span>
            <span>Disclosed, no adjustment to recognised amounts</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13">
      <span class="num">13</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 22</span>
            <span>Consolidated Financial Statements — relevant for subsidiary reporting flow considerations near the approval date</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14">
      <span class="num">14</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Adjusting event</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A subsequent event providing evidence of conditions existing at the balance sheet date, requiring adjustment to the financial statements.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Approval date (承認日)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The date financial statements are approved for issue, marking the end of the subsequent events review period.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
